[02:30.01] Ticking away the moments that make up a dull day
[02:37.04] You fritter and waste the hours in an offhand way
[02:44.43] Kicking around on a piece of ground in your hometown
[02:51.93] Waiting for someone or something to show you the way
[02:59.42] Tired of lying in the sunshine
[03:02.84] Staying home to watch the rain
[03:06.88] And you are young and life is long
[03:10.61] And there is time to kill today
[03:14.19] And then one day you find
[03:17.59] Ten years have got behind you
[03:22.36] No one told you when to run
[03:25.04] You missed the starting gun
[03:29.90] And you run, and you run to catch up with the sun
[03:35.06] 
[04:59.65] But it's sinking
[05:03.12] Racing around to come up behind you again
[05:08.67] 
[05:10.69] The sun is the same in a relative way
[05:13.86] But you're older
[05:17.52] Shorter of breath, and one day closer to death
[05:24.72] Every year is getting shorter
[05:28.24] Never seem to find the time
[05:31.68] Plans that either come to naught
[05:35.74] Or half a page of scribbled lines
[05:39.99] Hanging on in quiet desperation
[05:43.14] Is the English way
[05:47.74] The time is gone, the song is over
[05:50.99] Thought I'd something more to say
[05:55.42] 
[06:12.30] Home, home again
[06:17.10] 
[06:19.75] I like to be here when I can
[06:25.28] 
[06:27.75] When I come home cold and tired
[06:34.92] It's good to warm my bones beside the fire
[06:42.63] Far away, across the field
[06:45.87] The tolling of the iron bell
[06:50.15] Calls the faithful to their knees
[06:54.45] To hear the softly spoken magic spells
[06:58.44] 